      {
        "id": 143045,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-09-13T18:36:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Sounds to me like he's assuming GtG is focusing more on upcoming stuff than stuff that's already been paid for, which is probably true. &nbsp;The stuff that's already been paid for is more \"done\" than the upcoming stuff, so it requires less attention. &nbsp;If what someone cared about is what they've paid for and all they see is talk about upcoming stuff, I'll bet that's frustrating.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I bet you're right, at least about how the original poster feels, but there's being frustrated and then there's being frustrated and rude. The first is ok, and I want everyone to feel that the truth is valued here.</p>",
