      {
        "id": 143049,
        "name": "cmschex",
        "username": "cmschex",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/e9bcb4/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-10-01T16:39:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"godzilla999666\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/ccd318/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> godzilla999666:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>i'm sorry if you feel i was rude, i was very frustrated. I pre-ordered in Febraury and March like most of you, and for me the choice to pre-order meant that I went without other things. Since that time, at the time of post, we had a small update in June, and since that time, all the news was on new games, back us on this kickstarter and that one, not once by several times.&nbsp; Since it was september and 3 months had past, i was very worried that none of the preorder was going to be delivered in 2015 like they estimated. Now that they took the time to update, I know that I will get one of my pre-orders in October, another one maybe by end of year, and one pre-order (tactics:Broken city) will not be until next year. This is the second time i have pre-ordered/backed something that was not coming within the next month after ordering it. The first time, that money got flushed and the kickstater took off with the money, so I have extremely causious about doing any pre-order/backing, so yes I wanted to hear about what was happening on the stuff i put money on.&nbsp; I do not feel a simple post every month to two months is too much to ask for.&nbsp; When i made the comment about getting more money, the current state reminded me of a salesman. Yes i sold you this, now ignore it, and ignore where it is at, let me show you this over here and this over here.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>While I certainly understand your frustration and your caution, given your previous experience, I can say with nearly complete certainty that you will get your products from GtG, even if Tactics is delayed until 2016. &nbsp;They have always fulfilled (and in many cases fulfilled early). &nbsp;My guess on the communication is that the Dice Hate Me merger happened very soon after the pre-order and so a lot of the project update communication has been including those new lines that had previously not existed for the company, &nbsp;I think that these status updates are their attempt to do what you are asking for - a monthly update of their products in the pipeline. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
